Provenance
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

mos65 is a Go port of the 6502 assembler / simulator originally written
in JavaScript as `6502asm.com` by Stian Soreng (©2006–2010) and later
adapted by Nick Morgan as the `skilldrick/6502js` web app
(https://github.com/skilldrick/6502js).

The 6502 instruction set semantics, the assembler grammar (label syntax,
`define`, `DCB`, `*=` origin, `#<label` / `#>label`, addressing modes),
the memory-mapped screen at $0200–$05FF using the 16-colour palette,
the random-byte source at $FE and keyboard input at $FF, and the
behaviour of the included `testdata/snake.asm` program all derive from
those upstream projects.

Both upstream projects are licensed under the GNU General Public License
version 3. As a derivative work, mos65 is therefore released under the
same licence.
